# hoko configuration — the hoko.env layer.
#
# `hoko.json` is the file to edit: it holds every setting, the agent models included, and
# hoko.json.example names each key with its default. This file is optional: copy it to
# ~/.config/opencode/hoko.env (machine-local, survives a git pull) or to hoko.env in this
# repo to override what hoko.json sets, and to configure the plugin-only switches that
# have no hoko.json key — HOKO_FRESH_SESSION, HOKO_BASE_BRANCH and HOKO_PR_AUTO.
#
# Every setting has a working default, so an empty file is a valid configuration.
#
# Precedence, lowest first:
#   hoko.json in this repo  →  ~/.config/opencode/hoko.json
#   →  hoko.env in this repo  →  ~/.config/opencode/hoko.env  →  the real environment
#
# A line here overrides the same key in either hoko.json, and a HOKO_* variable in the
# real environment overrides every file:
#   HOKO_PLAN_MODEL=opencode-go/glm-5.3-flash
#
# The plugin exports every setting into each shell an agent runs, which is how the skills
# read them.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- models -----
# "provider/model-id" — run `opencode models` for the list. Leave a model unset and that
# agent uses whatever model the session is on.

# The planning agent: grills the request and writes the plan.
#HOKO_PLAN_MODEL=opencode-go/glm-5.3-flash

# The build agent: conducts a plan run or a /hoko/task run — decides on the gate's
# findings, dispatches every stage, commits. Also what plain build-mode chat runs on. In
# fresh mode the run happens in a fresh session, so it does not inherit the planning
# session's model; set this to pin it.
#HOKO_BUILD_MODEL=opencode-go/deepseek-v4-flash

# The executor subagent: implements one plan step at a time.
#HOKO_EXECUTOR_MODEL=opencode-go/deepseek-v4-flash

# The reviewer subagent: reviews a diff on request, outside a run.
#HOKO_REVIEWER_MODEL=opencode-go/glm-5.3-flash

# The final reviewer: the one review of a finished run, over the whole branch. Unset means
# it inherits whatever model the session supplied.
#HOKO_FINAL_REVIEW=opencode-go/deepseek-v4-flash

# The QA subagent: the end-of-run full gate, and it fixes what it finds.
#HOKO_QA_MODEL=opencode-go/glm-5.3-flash

# The research subagent: reads documentation and reports with citations.
#HOKO_RESEARCH_MODEL=opencode-go/deepseek-v4-flash


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- journal ----
# The journal root. One folder per cycle and per project holds the prompt, the plan,
# the closing report, the registered sessions, the usage and the token invoice.
# There is no default: leave this unset and nothing is journaled — the workflow itself
# is unaffected. Point it at a notes vault, a plain directory, wherever.
#HOKO_JOURNAL_PATH=~/notes/journal


# --------------------------------------------------------------- analytics ---
# Where the analytics folder goes: the session registry, the events copies and the invoice,
# under <analyticsPath>/<project>/<entry>/. Empty means they stay in the journal entry,
# which is the default — set it to keep the notes vault free of numbers. usage.json and
# rates.json stay in the journal entry either way, beside the report they priced.
#HOKO_ANALYTICS_PATH=/Users/you/ai/analytics/opencode


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- pipeline ---
# How many review rounds a task pipeline may run before it stops and asks. 0 accepts the
# open findings without asking.
#HOKO_LOOP_LIMIT=3

# Lint the plan at approval and refuse a plan with a blocking finding. Set to 0 to hand
# the plan over regardless.
#HOKO_PLAN_GATE=1

# Deny the conductor's own reads and edits of the repository while a run is in progress, so
# the step work stays with the subagents it launches. Set to 0 to switch the guard off.
#HOKO_LOOP_GUARD=1

# The spec pass: 1 makes a plan run reconcile the spec after the gate, and a task write
# specs/ before planning. Off by default — a task then keeps its spec as spec.md in its own
# folder.
#HOKO_SPECS=0


# ------------------------------------------------------------------ events ---
# Append the run's events to <eventsDir>/<run_id>/events.jsonl. Set to 0 to write none.
#HOKO_EVENTS=1

# Where the run event folders live, relative to the repository root.
#HOKO_EVENTS_DIR=.ai/runs


# ------------------------------------------------------------------ quality ---
# The CRAP index in the full quality gate, and the floor it holds to.
#HOKO_CRAP=1
#HOKO_CRAP_MAX=30

# Mutation testing in the full quality gate, and the minimum score it holds to.
#HOKO_MUTATION=1
#HOKO_MUTATION_MIN=70

# Price overrides as a JSON object, laid over the bundled pricing.json: one entry per model
# with input, output and cache rates per million tokens, for a model the table does not
# know or one it prices wrong.
#HOKO_PRICING={"provider/model": {"input": 1, "output": 2}}


# ------------------------------------------------------------------- plans ---
# Where plans are written, relative to the repository root. The plan agent may edit
# nothing else, so changing this moves the one path it can write. The top-level segment
# is what execute-plan adds to .gitignore when the repo does not already track it.
#HOKO_PLANS_DIR=.ai/plans


# ----------------------------------------------------------------- handoff ---
# Approving a plan starts the build run in a new session and switches the TUI to it, so
# the conductor's context is the plan file and nothing else. A fresh session is the
# default because the conductor reads the plan file, not the conversation, and dragging
# the planning transcript along is pure context cost. The planning session keeps its
# transcript and is left untouched. Set this to 0, false, no or off to queue the handoff
# on the approval session and run the plan there, as before.
#HOKO_FRESH_SESSION=1


# ------------------------------------------------------------------- gates ---
# The coverage floor the full quality gate holds to, as a percentage. A floor, not a
# target — the gate treats lowering it as a regression.
#HOKO_COVERAGE_MIN=85


# --------------------------------------------------------------- git flow ----
# Commit without asking for confirmation on the message (1 = on). The protected-branch
# check and the quality gate still apply, and pushing is never part of committing.
#HOKO_COMMIT_AUTO=1

# The branch that plays the `develop` role: what feature and bugfix branches are cut from
# and open their pull request against. Unset means `develop` when the repository has one
# and the remote's default branch when it does not, so a develop-flow repository needs
# nothing here. It never overrides a hotfix or release branch, which are cut from and
# target the release branch.
#HOKO_BASE_BRANCH=develop

# Push the branch and open the pull request without asking (1 = on). Left unset, the end
# of a run shows the base, branch and title and waits for confirmation. Only applies when
# origin is GitHub; any other remote leaves the branch for manual integration.
#HOKO_PR_AUTO=1


# ------------------------------------------------------- not read from here ---
# These two are opencode's own, read from the real environment at startup — the plugin
# cannot set them for you. Export them from your shell profile if you have leftover
# Claude Code files: opencode loads ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md as instructions and
# ~/.claude/skills/*/SKILL.md as skills, and an old copy of this workflow there will
# tell the model plans live in .claude/plans/.
#
#   export OPENCODE_DISABLE_CLAUDE_CODE_PROMPT=1
#   export OPENCODE_DISABLE_CLAUDE_CODE_SKILLS=1
